<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Fiery Cross Reef, 2021</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY text=#dcdcdc bgColor=#2b2b2b scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;CMO: Fiery Cross Reef/Spratly Islands, 2021&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Al "Beirutdude" Sandrik&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;The Time Is: 2 July 2021 00:00:00 Zulu/08:00:00 Hong Kong Time&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Last Edited:&amp;nbsp;5 September 2020&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Spratly Islands / South China Sea&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;Playable as the U.S./Allied Side&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;2&amp;nbsp;Days Duration&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Background:&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;EM&gt;The world is at war&lt;/EM&gt;… &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Three weeks ago, Iran attacked Al Udeid Air Force Base in Qatar with short and medium range ballistic missiles&amp;nbsp;resulting in&amp;nbsp;heavy loss of American, British and Qatari lives. The next day America struck back with a massive Tomahawk/PGM strike against Iranian bases near the Straits of Hormuz as well as across the Arabian Gulf. In short order, IRGC ballistic missile units, stationed in Syria and western Iran, launched on Israeli targets across the Golan and Galilee. Many of them were&amp;nbsp;intercepted by the IDF Arrow missile defense system; however, one intercepted warhead impacted an elementary school killing 131 Israeli school children,&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;47 teachers/staff and injured hundreds more. During the&amp;nbsp;subsequent Israeli response, and for the first time, the Russian S-400 Battery, near Latakia, engaged IAF aircraft shooting down five (5) F-16Is. An American strike, both in support of Israel and as a precursor to their own attack on Iranian assets in Syria, destroyed the S-400 battery and neutralized the Russian Air Force's Khmeinim Air Force Base. In response to this American escalation, Sunburn missiles, from the cruiser Moskva,&amp;nbsp;destroyed&amp;nbsp;the USS Iwo Jima (LHD-7) and USS New York (LPD-21), south of Cyprus, with hundreds of sailors and Marines killed or missing. The following morning, Russian ground forces surged across the borders of the Baltic States overrunning them&amp;nbsp;within a day&amp;nbsp;and Russian air forces launched heavy air attacks&amp;nbsp;against Norway, Poland, The Ukraine, Romania&amp;nbsp;and Turkey.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In the Far East, Kim-Jong-Un, backed by his nuclear warheads, saw&amp;nbsp;the opportunity to unify the peninsula under his rule. NKPA forces surged south overrunning portions of the northern ROK&amp;nbsp;by the end of the first&amp;nbsp;week. The North Korean Navy and Air Force were&amp;nbsp;hunted down and destroyed piece by piece by South Korean and JMSDF forces&amp;nbsp;prompting the Peoples Republic of China to intervene. The resulting "Second Battle of the Tsushima Straits"&amp;nbsp;ended with&amp;nbsp;a pyrrhic Western victory&amp;nbsp;with dozens of ships on both the PRC and South Korea/JMSDF/USN sides going to the bottom. Worse still for the West, the USS Ronald Reagan (CVN-76) was severely damaged by a DF-21D ASBM which&amp;nbsp;clipped the extreme aft portion of the flight deck. With severe damage she is currently limping to Bremerton, Washington for repairs. The loss of the Reagan&amp;nbsp;was achieved without the use of the PRC Carrier Liaoning (CV 16) or the new PLAN carrier&amp;nbsp;Shandong (CV 17). The surviving PLAN surface and submarine forces have largely retreated back to the protection of PRC air and SAM coverage, except in the South China Sea.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The front lines have now stabilized everywhere&amp;nbsp;except in&amp;nbsp;the Middle East, where IDF forces are driving into south Lebanon and toward Damascus.&amp;nbsp;The time has come for the West to take the offensive and the first move will&amp;nbsp;come against the PRC/PLA(N) with the Spratly/Paracel Islands as your target. Your Carrier Strike Group (CSG 9) is joining forward deployed USAF/USN Squadrons&amp;nbsp;in the Philippines and Australian Naval/Air Forces. You are&amp;nbsp;are tasked with destroying, or neutralizing, the recently constructed outposts on the South China Sea/Spratly Group reefs and islands, prior to&amp;nbsp;a planned amphibious assault/island-hopping campaign envisioned for them.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Notes: &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;DIR&gt;
&lt;DIR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Position: &lt;/STRONG&gt;American/Western forces are spread from Guam to near Singapore. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Course/Speed: &lt;/STRONG&gt;I have not set a course or speed for the USN-allied vessels as&amp;nbsp;I find it easier to set up missions if they are all oriented toward 360 degrees. Is it realistic? NO! However,&amp;nbsp;for game purposes&amp;nbsp;I believe it works.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Magazine load outs:&lt;/STRONG&gt; There are limited magazine load outs, especially in the Philippines, &lt;FONT color=red&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;that is deliberate please don’t go in the scenario editor and edit them!&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt; As a commander you are rarely going to have everything you want, &lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;or need&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;, for that matter. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Aircraft load outs: A&lt;/STRONG&gt;s of the tweaks on 08/30/2020, I have&amp;nbsp;readied/provided load outs for the&lt;STRONG&gt; land-based aircraft &lt;/STRONG&gt;(not the carrier). I&amp;nbsp;readied them&amp;nbsp;as I would load them out. Experienced players can go in the Scenario Editor and adjust the readied aircraft&amp;nbsp;as they see fit (within the limited magazine supplies please). Otherwise if you just reload the aircraft, yes you will have a 3/6/20 hour unavailable period, but it is the same as the original intent of the scenario. I just thought with the world at war it was just unrealistic that all of those aircraft would be spotted in a clean/unarmed state. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;If you do go into the scenario editor to edit the readied aircraft loadouts, please remember to update your .INI and .Delta files to reflect the new load outs for a rebuild. &lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;ADM-141 TALD&amp;nbsp;and ADM-160 MALD Series Drones:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/STRONG&gt;These must be launched with a Bearing Only Launch. The ADM-160J series jamming drones may be reprogramed in flight (a course plotted). I suggest you plot them with multiple passes across areas you want to jam. If they stop, you lose control of them, so word to the wise keep them flying!!!!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Missions:&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;A very limited number&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt; of air/vessel missions are&amp;nbsp;set up for the US/Allied side to keep things honest&amp;nbsp;at the beginning. Of course, please feel free to change/adjust them either during play or in the scenario editor, In fact I would very quickly take the F-15Cs OUT of the Luzon AAW / CAP Mission and set them up for their own mission! &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Teleporting: &lt;/STRONG&gt;Teleporting is conducted &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;1 second into the scenario starting&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; for technical reasons.&lt;STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/STRONG&gt;More specifically the PLAN surface groups need to teleport one second into the game to ensure their missions teleport with them (for some reason they don't seem to when teleported at the start). Therefore,&amp;nbsp;all units teleport at the same time to be consistent. Please run the scenario for about 5 seconds or so before setting up your missions. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Reference Points (RPs): &lt;/STRONG&gt;After&amp;nbsp;five (5), or more, seconds into the scenario (Teleports should be done by then), please feel free to delete the RPs highlighted "&lt;STRONG&gt;Teleport&lt;/STRONG&gt;" RPs to clean up the map. &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;IMPORTANT&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;! DO NOT delete the four locked reference points around the Scarborough Shoals (unless you don't want the victory points!),&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Scoring:&lt;/STRONG&gt; Almost everything destroyed will earn, &lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;or cost&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;, you Victory Points! Your mission is to destroy the PRC/PLAN position in the Spratlys with &lt;EM&gt;&lt;U&gt;minimal loss &lt;/U&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;to your own assets. I know some folks don’t like this about my scenarios, sorry but my experience has been the loss of units represents much more than just their military value, there is a political and psychological aspect to their loss which also must be accounted for. For example, who's heart doesn't skip a beat when the USS Enterprise (CV-6) or HMS Hood is sunk in a WWII game? They are more than just ships and planes, and that is especially true for the high value units&amp;nbsp;such as&amp;nbsp;the carriers. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Playtesting: &lt;/STRONG&gt;I have tweaked this scenario&amp;nbsp;substantially with a lot of support from DReese, AndrewJ, Maji, Excroat, and a few others. Thank you.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Hope you enjoy it. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIR&gt;&lt;/DIR&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=""&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Originally created under CMO Version 1115.8.1 – Data Base: DB3000 480&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Last Updated 08/30/2020 to CMO Version&amp;nbsp;1147.4.0 -&amp;nbsp;Data Base DB3000 483&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;An .INI and .Delta File have both been provided for rebuilds&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Al "BeirutDude" Sandrik (ex-Beachinnole)&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
